      "candidate": "```yaml\n# Repaired scraper configuration\nschema: gpu-price-schema-v1\n\nscraper:\n  # Extract the product id from the page URL\n  product_id:\n    selector: \"body\"\n    attribute: \"data-product-id\"\n    postprocess: >-\n      return extract_from_url(context['url'])\n\n  # Extract the product title\n  title:\n    selector: \"h1.product-title\"\n    type: \"text\"\n\n  # Extract the price \u2013 the selector changed to the new #price element.\n  price:\n    selector: \"#price\"\n    type: \"text\"\n    # Grab the numeric part (e.g.\u202f$599.99 \u2192 599.99)\n    regex: \"\\\\d+(?:[\\\\.,]\\\\d+)?\"\n    # Convert the string to a float\n    postprocess: |\n      import re\n      m = re.search(r'\\\\d+(?:[\\\\.,]\\\\d+)?', context['value'])\n      return float(m.group(0).replace(',', '.'))\n\n  # Extract the rating \u2013 use a data\u2011attribute that now holds the numeric value\n  rating:\n    selector: \"div.rating-stars span[data-rating]\"\n    attribute: \"data-rating\"\n    type: \"float\"\n\n# Fallbacks (in case the new selector fails)\nfallbacks:\n  - field: price\n    selector: \"span.price\"\n    type: \"text\"\n    regex: \"\\\\d+(?:[\\\\.,]\\\\d+)?\"\n  - field: rating\n    selector: \"span.rating\"\n    type: \"text\"\n    regex: \"\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?\"\n```\n\n**What changed**\n\n* Updated the **price selector** from the old `.product-price` element to the new `#price` element.\n* Added a **regex** to strip out currency symbols and a **post\u2011processing** step to convert the extracted text to a numeric float.\n* Updated the **rating selector** to pull the value from the new `data-rating` attribute on the `<span>` element.\n* Kept the rest of the extraction logic identical to preserve the `gpu-price-schema-v1` output format."
